---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Harvey Brooks — Editor | CreditDoc"
  description="Harvey Brooks is the editor overseeing selected hand-reviewed lender profiles on CreditDoc."
  canonical="https://www.creditdoc.co/about/harvey-brooks/"
>
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
    <nav class="text-sm text-muted mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-primary">Home</a> <span class="mx-2">/</span>
      <a href="/about/" class="hover:text-primary">About</a> <span class="mx-2">/</span>
      <span>Harvey Brooks</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2">Harvey Brooks</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-muted mb-8">Editor, CreditDoc</p>

    <section class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
      <h2>Role</h2>
      <p>
        Harvey Brooks serves as editor for selected CreditDoc hand-reviewed
        lender profiles. His role is to check written profile content against
        provider websites, regulator records, and other cited public sources
        before publication.
      </p>

      <h2>Scope of Editorial Review</h2>
      <p>
        Editorial review at CreditDoc is reserved for a limited flagship
        profile set. Most lender pages are automatically compiled from public
        regulatory filings (including NCUA, FDIC, and HUD records) and
        publicly available business information.
      </p>

      <h2>What Editorial Review Is</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Written review facts are source-checked against the lender's own website or a primary-source regulator where available</li>
        <li>Products, pricing tiers, fees, and eligibility criteria are checked against available sources</li>
        <li>Pros and cons are written from observed source material rather than generic boilerplate</li>
        <li>The profile is published after editorial checks are complete, while readers should still verify current provider terms directly</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What Editorial Review Is Not</h2>
      <p>
        Editorial review does <strong>not</strong> set the star rating.
        When a star rating is shown on CreditDoc, it uses the stored Google
        rating with the stored Google review count. If reliable Google rating
        data is unavailable, no star rating is shown. See our
        <a href="/methodology/">methodology page</a> for how editorial review
        and rating display work.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        For editorial corrections or feedback, please use the contact form
        on our <a href="/about/">About page</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12 rounded-xl border border-border bg-white p-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text mb-4">Use This Editor Page With CreditDoc Context</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">
        Editorial review is one layer in the wider CreditDoc graph. These pages explain the data, methodology, and research context behind public profiles.
      </p>
      <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <a href="/methodology/" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-alt p-4 hover:border-primary/40">
          <span class="block text-sm font-semibold text-text">Methodology</span>
          <span class="mt-1 block text-xs text-muted">How CreditDoc organizes profiles, ratings display, and comparison context.</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/editorial-policy/" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-alt p-4 hover:border-primary/40">
          <span class="block text-sm font-semibold text-text">Editorial Policy</span>
          <span class="mt-1 block text-xs text-muted">How corrections, updates, and editorial independence are handled.</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/about/creditdoc-data/" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-alt p-4 hover:border-primary/40">
          <span class="block text-sm font-semibold text-text">CreditDoc Data</span>
          <span class="mt-1 block text-xs text-muted">How public records and provider data feed directory pages.</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/research/consumer-complaints/" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-alt p-4 hover:border-primary/40">
          <span class="block text-sm font-semibold text-text">Complaint Data</span>
          <span class="mt-1 block text-xs text-muted">Use public complaint patterns as one research input.</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
